{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And HaShem spoke to Moses on Mount Sinai.</b> Now, Scripture does not mention the place of commandment for any commandment, unless something novel occurred then in that place. Rather, it explains that when the Exalted El said at Sinai (Exodus 23:11), ״וְהַשְּׁבִיעִת תִּשְׁמְטֶנָּה וּנְטַשְׁתָּהּ וְאָכְלוּ אֶבְיֹנֵי עַמֶּךָ וְיִתְרָם וְכוּ׳״, He then explained to Moses all the laws of the sabbatical year stated here. And this is to understand and to instruct that this was likewise the case for all the other commandments: even though the verse for some of them is brief, the explanation at that time was broad and thoroughly expounded, as they said, of blessed memory (Torat Kohanim 1:1): ״מָה עִנְיַן שְׁמִטָּה לְעִנְיַן הַר סִינַי? אֶלָּא מָה שְׁמִטָּה נֶאֶמְרוּ כְּלָלוֹתֶיהָ וּפֵרוּשֶׁיהָ וְדִקְדּוּקֶיהָ מִסִּינַי, אַף כָּל הַמִּצְווֹת נֶאֶמְרוּ מִסִּינַי כְּלָלוֹתֵיהֶם וְדִקְדּוּקֵיהֶם וּפֵרוּשֵׁיהֶם״. And Moses our teacher placed this passage here, because he thought they would soon enter the land, as he testified in saying (Numbers 10:29) ״נֹסְעִים אֲנַחְנוּ אֶל הַמָּקוֹם״. And he warned specifically about the sabbatical year of the land, because through their sin in failing to keep it they would be exiled from it, as he testified in saying (Leviticus 26:34) ״אָז תִּרְצֶה הָאָרֶץ אֶת שַׁבְּתֹתֶיהָ״, and likewise he testified at the end of Chronicles in saying (2 Chronicles 36:21) ״עַד רָצְתָה הָאָרֶץ אֶת שַׁבְּתוֹתֶיהָ״."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:37:53.181377898Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}